{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01USnqsJeknJozXPCnqgrbmK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Project State Summary\n\n**Problem**: go-unix-utils reimplements GNU coreutils/moreutils in Go, verified via differential testing against Homebrew reference binaries. It's a stress test for specification-driven AI code generation.\n\n**Architecture**: `cmd/<name>/` holds one utility each (main.go + tests). `pkg/testutils/` provides differential testing. `pkg/sys/` wraps syscalls. `pkg/format/` handles output formatting. `pkg/hashutil/`, `pkg/sizeparse/`, `pkg/encutil/` provide shared hash/size/encoding logic. SRDs in `docs/specs/` are the source of truth.\n\n**Current state**: 33 releases (00.0–15.0), ~70 utilities implemented, ~40 remaining. Many releases are fully implemented; gaps are scattered across releases.\n\n**Current release focus**: `requirement_states` shows only two SRDs with \"ready\" requirements:\n- **srd110-pr** (release 15.0): R3.1, R4.1, R4.2, R4.3, R5.1, R5.2 — all ready\n- **srd111-ptx** (release 15.0): R3.1, R4.1, R4.2, R5.1, R5.2 — all ready\n\nBoth pr and ptx have codestatus \"not started\" in release 15.0. ts and stty (same release) are already implemented.\n\n## Priority Analysis\n\nPer P1, I focus on the earliest incomplete release with ready requirements — release 15.0. Within 15.0, pr (cmd/pr, srd110) comes before ptx (cmd/ptx, srd111) alphabetically (P8). With a 4-task limit and the requirement to split implementation from tests (P2), I can fully cover pr (6 requirements across 4 tasks) and defer ptx to the next batch.\n\n## Weight Budget Check\n\nAssuming default weight=1 for all sub-requirements (requirements.yaml not in project_context):\n\n```\nTask 0: R3.1(w=1) + R4.1(w=1) + R4.2(w=1) + R4.3(w=1) = 4 ≤ 4 ✓\nTask 1: R5.1(w=1) + R5.2(w=1) = 2 ≤ 4 ✓\nTask 2: R3.1(w=1) + R4.1(w=1) + R4.2(w=1) + R4.3(w=1) = 4 ≤ 4 ✓\nTask 3: R5.1(w=1) + R5.2(w=1) = 2 ≤ 4 ✓\n```\n\n## Propose